  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-montezumae-2/",
      "html": "<p>With the swordtails (Xiphophorus), the males carry a sword-like extension at the low end of the tail fin in many species. This is a luxury structure that serves intraspecific communication. Sword-bearing males appear especially sexy to the females and especially intimidating to male conspecifics. The game \"who has the longest\", well known also among primates (the ape-like animals), is always won by Xiphophorus montezumae with its sword.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-montezumae-2/",
      "html": "<p>This magnificent swordtail has a comparatively limited distribution area in nature (rivers in the state of San Luis Potosí, on the Atlantic side of Mexico).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-montezumae-2/",
      "html": "<p>For the care it is important to pay attention to constantly good water quality. Generous weekly partial water changes are therefore absolutely necessary.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-montezumae-2/",
      "html": "<p>The Montezuma swordtail prefers relatively low temperatures (18-22°C) for permanent keeping – it does no harm if the temperatures climb above 24°C in summer. The water should preferably be hard and the pH should be in the slightly alkaline range (8 – 8.5).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-montezumae-2/",
      "html": "<p>A good flake food can be the nutritional basis; in addition one feeds frozen and live food of all kinds. Regular feeding of Artemia nauplii (also to adult fish, 2-3 times a week) has proved very successful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus-montezumae-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species is by far not as productive as, for example, Green Swordtails (X. hellerii); the litters usually include much fewer than 20 young. Since it prefers low temperatures, it grows rather slowly. This explains why this beauty will always remain a rarity in the hobby.</p>"
    }
  ],
